  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Support to enhance manufacturing capacities and access to vaccines, medicines and health technologies in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives pursued by this special measure action is to to advance country level intervention in Egypt deemed critical for reinforcing local manufacturing capacities and creating an improved access to health products in Africa. It is a part of Team Europe Initiative on Manufacturing and Access to Vaccines, Medicines and Health Technologies (TEI MAV+) for Sub-Saharan Africa, which expanded to North Africa in collaboration with DG INTPA. This will be implemented under INTPA (ACT-62262) which include the support to other African countries.  The action will support the development of an enabling environment for pharmaceutical products and health technologies in Egypt, with a primary focus on responding to the concrete needs identified, notably skills development, support to the regulatory authority, technology transfers, and ensuring demand for locally produced goods complementing continental and regional level actions. It will also reinforce the dialogue established between Team Europe and Egypt&#xBF;s Governments on this matter.</narrative>
  </description>
